ames>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Beier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tautz</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tests of rRNA hybridization to microarrays suggest that hybridization characteristics of oligonucleotide probes for species discrimination cannot be predicted</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Research</source><year>2006</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>e66</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16707658</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/nar/gkl133</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naiser</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Mai</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Michel</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Ott</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Versatile maskless microscope projection photolithography system and its application in light-directed fabrication of DNA microarrays</article-title><source>Review of Scientific Instruments</source><year>2006</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>063711</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1063/1.2213152</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naiser</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kayser</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mai</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Michel</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Ott</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impact of point-mutations on the hybridization affinity of surface-bound DNA/DNA and RNA/DNA oligonucleotide duplexes: comparison of single base mismatches and base bulges</article-title><source>BMC Biotechnology</source><year>2008</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>48</fpage><pub-id pub-id-